@startuml SplitSmartArchitectureBSystemContext
title Architecture B - Web-First System Context
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Account holder" as user
actor "Group organizer" as organizer
actor "Reviewer" as reviewer

rectangle "SplitSmart web-first product" as product {
  component "Web client" as web
  component "Android client" as android
  component "iOS client" as ios
  component "Versioned REST API" as api
  component "Modular application backend" as backend
  database "Shared PostgreSQL data" as db
}

cloud "Email provider" as email
cloud "Receipt object storage" as storage

user --> web
user --> android
user --> ios
organizer --> web
reviewer --> web
web --> api : HTTPS
android --> api : HTTPS
ios --> api : HTTPS
api --> backend
backend --> db
backend --> storage : receipt objects
backend --> email : verification/reset only

note right of product
Architecture B is the full-product web-first alternative.
The Java Swing MVP remains a separate decision in Architecture A.
end note
@enduml
